    "file": "ndpi/src/lib/protocols/fix.c",
    "description": "Heap out-of-bounds read in FIX dissector: ndpi_search_fix unconditionally reads packet->payload[0..5] after only checking packet->tcp, without validating packet->payload_packet_len >= 6. For short TCP payloads, this reads past the end of the input buffer and crashes under ASan.",
    "conditions": "In fuzz_process_packet, attacker-controlled input is passed to ndpi_detection_process_packet, which routes TCP packets with nonzero payload into check_ndpi_tcp_flow_func and invokes ndpi_search_fix. If the packet is classified as TCP and reaches FIX detection with payload length less than 6 bytes (or truncated relative to expected FIX prefix checks), ndpi_search_fix performs unchecked byte accesses (payload[0..5]), causing a 1-byte heap-buffer-overflow read at fix.c:38."
